    "rationale": "Successor to 2.1 and 2.2 (owner choice of 2026-10-22), frozen before any confirmation data is read; the 2.1 and 2.2 failures stay on record. 2.2's reference, the bf16-tp8 profile, reproduces B200 arithmetic (#12404) and so did not sample cross-hardware variation, and with 14 retained router scores its own changed expert sets were partly unresolved. 2.3's reference is the CPU port's plain BF16 profile (cpu-bf16, no B200 emulation), a different implementation on different hardware from both the oracle and the candidate. Its oracle keeps all 384 router scores. Limits are HEADROOM times what that reference shows against the B200 oracle, judged per case and mode; the router rule is the margin and regret rule with a per-layer score budget in the selection function's units, an empirical connected budget rather than a rigorous bound. h1-h6 are exposed and serve only as reference and regression cases; the confirmation corpus is the generalization test.",
